      "created_at": "2015-03-01T15:43:36.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>You check range from the Origin. For a Vertex Area Attack, you choose the origin as you would for any standard Area Attack. Then you choose two other adjacent hexes touching a vertex of the origin. There's your area. On level ground, the range to the other two hexes is 1, but elevation could change that.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Unless something changed in the final rules. I'll confess I don't have the printed rulebook in front of me.</p>",
